{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"files\":[{\"content\":\"#define _POSIX_C_SOURCE 200112L\\n#include <stdint.h>\\n#include <stdio.h>\\n#include <stdlib.h>\\n\\n#define CONV_THRESHOLD 1.0e-5f\\n\\nstatic double *grid;\\nstatic double *new_grid;\\nstatic size_t row_stride;\\nstatic int size;\\nstatic int iter_max_num;\\n\\nstatic double absolute(double num) {\\n    if (num < 0)\\n        return -1.0 * num;\\n    return num;\\n}\\n\\nstatic int allocate_memory(void) {\\n    size_t n = (size_t)size;\\n    if (n > SIZE_MAX - 7u)\\n        return 0;\\n    row_stride = (n + 7u) & ~(size_t)7u;\\n    if (row_stride > SIZE_MAX / n / sizeof(double))\\n        return 0;\\n\\n    size_t bytes = row_stride * n * sizeof(double);\\n    if (posix_memalign((void **)&grid, 64, bytes) != 0)\\n        return 0;\\n    if (posix_memalign((void **)&new_grid, 64, bytes) != 0) {\\n        free(grid);\\n        grid = NULL;\\n        return 0;\\n    }\\n    return 1;\\n}\\n\\nstatic void initialize_grid(void) {\\n    int center = size / 2;\\n    int linf = center - (size / 10);\\n    int lsup = center + (size / 10);\\n    for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) {\\n        size_t row = (size_t)i * row_stride;\\n        for (int j = 0; j < size; j++) {\\n            double value;\\n            if (i >= linf && i <= lsup && j >= linf && j <= lsup)\\n                value = 100;\\n            else\\n                value = 0;\\n            grid[row + (size_t)j] = value;\\n            new_grid[row + (size_t)j] = value;\\n        }\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nstatic void save_grid(void) {\\n    for (int i = 0; i < size; i++) {\\n        size_t row = (size_t)i * row_stride;\\n        for (int j = 0; j < size; j++)\\n            fprintf(stdout, \\\"%lf \\\", grid[row + (size_t)j]);\\n        fprintf(stdout, \\\"\\\\n\\\");\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nint main(int argc, char *argv[]) {\\n    (void)argc;\\n    (void)argv;\\n\\n    fscanf(stdin, \\\"%d\\\", &size);\\n    fscanf(stdin, \\\"%d\\\", &iter_max_num);\\n\\n    if (size <= 0)\\n        return 0;\\n    if (!allocate_memory())\\n        return 1;\\n    initialize_grid();\\n\\n    int hasError = 1;\\n    int iter = 0;\\n    while (hasError && iter < iter_max_num) {\\n        hasError = 0;\\n        for (int i = 1; i < size - 1; i++) {\\n            size_t row = (size_t)i * row_stride;\\n            for (int j = 1; j < size - 1; j++) {\\n                size_t k = row + (size_t)j;\\n                new_grid[k] = 0.25 * (grid[k + 1] + grid[k - 1] +\\n                                      grid[k - row_stride] + grid[k + row_stride]);\\n                double errorCurrent = absolute(new_grid[k] - grid[k]);\\n                if (errorCurrent > CONV_THRESHOLD)\\n                    hasError = 1;\\n            }\\n        }\\n\\n        double *temp = grid;\\n        grid = new_grid;\\n        new_grid = temp;\\n        iter++;\\n    }\\n\\n    save_grid();\\n    free(grid);\\n    free(new_grid);\\n    return 0;\\n}\\n\",\"path\":\"src/laplace_seq.c\"}],\"hypothesis\":\"A 64-byte-aligned contiguous layout with each row padded to a cache-line multiple should keep row starts aligned and reduce cache-line splits for arbitrary widths; swapping the two buffers avoids the interior copy while preserving Jacobi updates.\",\"notes\":\"Both buffers receive identical initial values so fixed boundaries remain unchanged after swaps, including for grids with no interior cells. The stencil expression order and output formatting are preserved. Research was not requested.\",\"research\":{\"queries\":[],\"urls\":[]},\"sources_kept\":[],\"transformations\":[\"Allocate two contiguous buffers on 64-byte boundaries and pad the row stride to a multiple of eight doubles.\",\"Use the padded stride for initialization, stencil access, and output while leaving padding cells unused.\",\"Swap source and destination buffers after each Jacobi iteration instead of copying interior cells.\" ]}"}}
